ed to MRI and two-photon microscopy data.</li>\n<li><strong>Single-Cell Omics</strong> — Scalable pipelines integrating multi-modal single-cell genomics and spatial transcriptomics.</li>\n<li><strong>Explainable AI in Neuroscience</strong> — Frameworks to probe decision boundaries and feature attributions in black-box models.</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>Selected Projects</h2>\n<div class='cards'>\n<div class='card'><h3>DeepVision</h3><p>High-Resolution Neural Activity Mapping. A PyTorch pipeline to segment two-photon images of mouse visual cortex with temporal convolutional networks; deployed as a Dockerized microservice with Cascade Imaging Lab.</p></div>\n<div class='card'><h3>NeuroGraph</h3><p>Graph Neural Networks for Circuit Analysis. Graph representations of EM neuron meshes; GNNs classify synapse types and infer connectivity motifs. Released in the NeuroTools suite.</p></div>\n<div class='card'><h3>CellMap</h3><p>Multi-Modal Single-Cell Atlas. A Nextflow workflow combining scRNA-Seq, ATAC-Seq, and spatial FISH data with Bayesian clustering; presented at ICSCG 2023.</p></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>Teaching &amp; Mentorship</h2>\n<ul class='list'>\n<li><strong>Undergraduate Course</strong> — 'Introduction to Computational Neuroscience' (Spring 2025).</li>\n<li><strong>Graduate Seminar</strong> — 'Advanced Machine Learning Methods in Biology' (Fall 2024).</li>\n<li><strong>Mentorship</strong> — Supervised 8 Ph.D. students and 12 Master's theses.</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>Skills &amp; Tools</h2>\n<div class='contact-grid'>\n<div><span>Languages</span>Python, R, C++</div>\n<div><span>Frameworks</span>PyTorch, TensorFlow, scikit-learn, NetworkX</div>\n<div><span>Data Tools</span>Nextflow, Snakemake, Docker, Kubernetes</div>\n<div><span>Analysis</span>MATLAB, Jupyter, Seurat, Scanpy</div>\n<div><span>Visualization</span>D3.js, Plotly, Matplotlib</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section>\n<h2>Contact</h2>\n<div class='contact-grid'>\n<div><span>Email</span><a href='mailto:lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu'>lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu</a></div>\n<div><span>Office</span>Blakely Hall, Room 312, Riverbend University</div>\n<div><span>Twitter</span><a href='https://twitter.com/LydiaNeuroLab'>@LydiaNeuroLab</a></div>\n<div><span>GitHub</span><a href='https://github.com/lydia-moreno'>github.com/lydia-moreno</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</main>\n<footer>\n<div class='container'>\n<span>© 2025 Dr. Lydia Moreno</span>\n<span><a href='index.html'>Back to home</a></span>\n</div>\n</footer>\n</body>\n</html>\nEOF\n",
